│ patch_name               │ add_entangling_crz_and_zzz_layers                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz relies solely on fixed (non-parametric) CZ gates for entanglement,     │
│                          │ sandwiched between two single-qubit rotation layers. This limits how much the entangling  │
│                          │ structure can be tuned during training, likely capping expressivity and validation        │
│                          │ accuracy. I add a lightly-parametrized entangling layer using CRZ gates with heavy        │
│                          │ parameter sharing (3 shared parameters spread over the same 12 allowed two-qubit pairs,   │
│                          │ grouped into 3 groups of 4 edges each) right after the existing CZ layer. This lets the   │
│                          │ model learn entanglement strength cheaply (only 3 extra parameters per block) while       │
│                          │ preserving most of the fixed structural connectivity. I also add two three-qubit ZZZ      │
│                          │ gates (sharing a single parameter) spanning distant qubit triples (0,4,8) and (1,5,6) to  │
│                          │ inject cheap higher-order correlations that single/two-qubit gates cannot capture, at the │
│                          │ cost of only 1 extra parameter. This should improve expressivity and validation accuracy  │
│                          │ without a large parameter blowup, keeping parameter efficiency reasonable.                │
