│                          │ To increase representational power without dramatically increasing parameter count, I     │
│                          │ insert three parametrized three-qubit ZZZ interaction gates (allowed on any qubit triple) │
│                          │ after the existing CZ entangling layer. These gates couple qubits that are not directly   │
│                          │ linked by the fixed 2-qubit topology (e.g. bridging separate CZ clusters), letting the    │
│                          │ circuit capture higher-order correlations relevant to the (unknown) data structure. Only  │
│                          │ 3 extra parameters per repetition are added (18 total across the 6 repetitions implied by │
│                          │ n_params=162), keeping the parameter-efficiency cost low while directly targeting the     │
│                          │ underfitting issue via increased circuit expressivity.                                    │
