│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz applies only RY then RZ rotations per qubit before entangling, which   │
│                          │ does not span the full single-qubit rotation group (missing an X-axis component). Adding  │
│                          │ an RX layer prior to the RY layer turns each qubit's local unitary into an RX‑RY‑RZ       │
│                          │ product, which is capable of representing an arbitrary single-qubit rotation (up to       │
│                          │ global phase). This should increase the model's expressive power and help address the     │
│                          │ current underfitting symptom (train accuracy only 0.57), without an excessive parameter   │
│                          │ increase (adds 9 parameters per block instantiation). The three-layer single qubit        │
│                          │ rotation combined with the existing entangling CZ pattern should give the circuit more    │
│                          │ capacity to fit the data while keeping the well-tested entangling topology unchanged.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Argumentation: Since generalization gap is small (0.07) but overall accuracy is quite low │
│                          │ (train ~0.57, val ~0.55, test ~0.49), the model appears to be underfitting rather than    │
│                          │ overfitting. Adding expressivity to the single-qubit rotation stage is a natural way to   │
│                          │ increase capacity without changing the entangling qubit-pair topology (which is           │
│                          │ architecturally fixed by hardware constraints), and is a standard technique in            │
│                          │ variational circuit design (using a universal single-qubit rotation decomposition         │
│                          │ RX-RY-RZ instead of just RY-RZ).                                                          │
