│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ learnable_entangling_crz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses fixed CZ gates for entanglement, meaning the entangling structure │
│                          │ is non-trainable and identical across all layers. This wastes representational capacity:  │
│                          │ the single-qubit rotations must compensate for a fixed, potentially mismatched entangling │
│                          │ pattern. I replace the fixed CZ gates with parametrized CRZ gates that share a single     │
│                          │ learnable parameter per repetition ("crz_ent"), allowing the model to learn the strength  │
│                          │ of entanglement (from ~0 essentially identity to full CZ-like behavior) while adding only │
│                          │ one extra parameter per block repetition (6 total across the circuit, from 162 to 168     │
│                          │ params). This is a low-risk, low-parameter-cost change that gives the optimizer control   │
│                          │ over entanglement strength, which can help match the actual correlation structure of the  │
│                          │ data, potentially improving accuracy while keeping the train-test gap and parameter       │
│                          │ efficiency good.                                                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
