│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The previous experiment showed that replacing fixed CZ gates with parametrized CRZ        │
│                          │ rotations (removing the wasteful RZ_pre layer) achieved the best score (0.59), clearly    │
│                          │ outperforming both the pure-CZ seed (0.52) and the version that added RZ_pre plus ZZZ     │
│                          │ three-qubit terms (0.55, likely too deep/overparametrized without added benefit).         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Building on the winning CRZ design, this edit removes the RZ_pre layer and the ZZZ        │
│                          │ three-qubit interactions (which hurt performance and added depth) and instead promotes    │
│                          │ the remaining 6 fixed CZ gates to parametrized CRY rotations. Using two different         │
│                          │ rotation axes (CRZ on one set of pairs, CRY on the other) increases the expressivity of   │
│                          │ the entangling layer along complementary directions of the Bloch sphere without adding    │
│                          │ extra circuit depth (still one two-qubit gate per allowed pair), which should better      │
│                          │ capture correlations in the data while keeping the circuit as shallow as the              │
│                          │ best-performing variant so far.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the qubit-pair connectivity identical to the seed/best version but makes every │
│                          │ entangling interaction trainable, which should improve accuracy at a modest parameter     │
│                          │ cost while avoiding the overfitting/depth issues seen when adding ZZZ+RZ_pre.             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0595                                                                                   │
