│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ param_sharing_hub_reduction                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current version turned three previously-fixed CZ gates (0,8), (1,8), (2,6) into fully │
│                          │ independent CRZ gates, raising the parameter count from 150 to 180. This increased train  │
│                          │ accuracy (0.75) but widened the generalization gap (0.14) and lowered validation accuracy │
│                          │ (0.65) compared to the 150-parameter seed (gap 0.09, val 0.66). This suggests the extra   │
│                          │ free parameters are overfitting rather than helping.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Instead of reverting these edges to non-parametrized CZ gates (losing expressivity        │
│                          │ entirely), we share their rotation parameter with an existing CRZ that shares the same    │
│                          │ hub qubit: (0,8) shares "crz_2" with (0,7), (1,8) shares "crz_3" with (1,3), and (2,6)    │
│                          │ shares "crz_4" with (2,4). This keeps the entangling gates parametrized (preserving some  │
│                          │ flexibility from the encoded data) while cutting the parameter count back to 150,         │
│                          │ matching the well-generalizing seed's budget. Sharing within a hub's outgoing edges is a  │
│                          │ natural symmetry prior: it encodes that a qubit's coupling strength to its neighbors is   │
│                          │ governed by one learned "hub activity" parameter, which should reduce overfitting and     │
│                          │ shrink the train/validation gap while retaining entangling coverage that the previous     │
│                          │ experiment lacked.                                                                        │
