│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Builds on the best-performing mixed CRZ/CRY pairwise-entangling ansatz (score 0.60) by    │
│                          │ adding: (1) a single shared RX "mixing" rotation across all 9 qubits (only 1 extra unique │
│                          │ parameter) to introduce X-axis diversity absent from the previous RY/RZ-only design, and  │
│                          │ (2) three CCRZ three-qubit interaction gates on triples that partition all 9 qubits       │
│                          │ exactly once ([0,5,6], [1,4,7], [2,3,8]), giving the circuit access to higher-order       │
│                          │ correlations that the restricted 2-qubit connectivity graph cannot express directly. The  │
│                          │ pairwise CRZ/CRY entangling layer and the RY encoding / RZ output layers are kept         │
│                          │ identical to the best prior design so as not to lose established gains. Total unique      │
│                          │ parameters increase modestly from 30 to 34 (204 trainable with the fixed x6 repetition    │
│                          │ factor), aiming to reduce the generalization gap and boost validation/test accuracy       │
│                          │ through richer, more global correlations rather than simply adding more pairwise          │
│                          │ capacity.                                                                                 │
