│ patch_name               │ add_ry_midlayer_prune_cz                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Based on the recommendation to reallocate trainable capacity from less-central entangling │
│                          │ gates toward single-qubit rotations, I prune the two least-central fixed CZ gates (edges  │
│                          │ [4,8] and [6,7], which are peripheral connections in the entangling graph) and insert a   │
│                          │ lightweight mid-circuit RY sublayer on qubits [1,3,5,7,8] with unique parameters          │
│                          │ (ry_mid_0…ry_mid_4). This keeps overall gate count and depth roughly comparable while     │
│                          │ giving the circuit more expressive single-qubit capacity right after the first entangling │
│                          │ block, which should help it fit richer feature combinations without over-relying on the   │
│                          │ two weakest entangling links. This builds directly on the proven RY→entangler→RZ sandwich │
│                          │ structure already in the ansatz, inserting the new RY layer between the CRZ chain and the │
│                          │ final RZ layer.                                                                           │
