│ patch_name               │ revert_to_cry_variant_with_crx_swap                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz (extra ZZZ terms, doubled CZ+CRZ layers) increased depth and parameter │
│                          │ count significantly (88 depth, 186 params) but achieved a lower combined score (0.56)     │
│                          │ than the simpler CRY-based variant (0.60) that used only 180 parameters and depth 41.     │
│                          │ This suggests the extra complexity is hurting generalization rather than helping          │
│                          │ expressivity. I revert to the higher-performing CRY-based structure and additionally      │
│                          │ apply the earlier recommendation: swap the CRY gate on wires (0,8) for a CRX gate,        │
│                          │ introducing axis diversity in the entangling layer while keeping the same gate count and  │
│                          │ depth. This should preserve the good generalization gap of the CRY variant while          │
│                          │ potentially improving expressivity through mixed-axis entanglement.                       │
