│ patch_description        │ The previous experiment (mixed CRZ/CRX, 180 params) scored lower (0.58) than the version  │
│                          │ using CRZ/CRY (180 params, 0.60) and the lean 150-param seed (0.60, smaller               │
│                          │ generalization gap). This suggests: (1) CRY is a better choice than CRX for the second    │
│                          │ entangling axis on this dataset, and (2) reducing parameter count (especially in the      │
│                          │ redundant post-entanglement RZ layer) tends to shrink the generalization gap without      │
│                          │ hurting accuracy. This edit reverts CRX->CRY (restoring the better-performing entangling  │
│                          │ layer) and additionally shares the 9 independent post-RZ rotation parameters into 5       │
│                          │ grouped parameters (pairing structurally similar/adjacent qubits), cutting per-block      │
│                          │ parameter count from 30 to 26 while keeping the same gate count and depth. This should    │
│                          │ retain expressivity from the entangling layer while reducing overfitting risk, aiming to  │
│                          │ combine the best traits of both prior high-scoring variants.                              │
