│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ revert_to_shared_crz_plus_zzz                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The previous edit (adding a mid RY sub-layer and replacing some CRZ entanglers with fixed │
│                          │ CZ) regressed performance (0.57 vs 0.63 for the shared-CRZ design). Revert the entangling │
│                          │ layer back to the proven parameter-shared CRZ scheme (which achieved combined score 0.63  │
│                          │ with 162 params), and additionally inject a small amount of genuine three-body            │
│                          │ correlation via a disjoint-qubit ZZZ layer using a single shared parameter. Because the   │
│                          │ three ZZZ gates act on completely disjoint qubit triples ((0,4,8),(1,3,6),(2,5,7)), they  │
│                          │ can be scheduled in parallel, adding only ~1 layer of depth and just 1 new parameter,     │
│                          │ while giving the ansatz access to third-order correlations across all 9 qubits that pure  │
│                          │ single/two-qubit rotations cannot capture. This should improve expressivity/accuracy      │
│                          │ without materially harming the train-test gap or convergence.                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0751                                                                                   │
