│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz (with extra CRY gates, shared RX mixing layer, and a CCRZ 3-qubit      │
│                          │ layer) increased depth to 63 and gate count to 279, which hurt generalization (train/val  │
│                          │ gap widened to 0.18, test accuracy dropped to 0.60, combined score fell to 0.56) compared │
│                          │ to the earlier, simpler 12-CRZ-gate ansatz that scored 0.63 with depth 41.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit reverts to the leaner, better-performing structure (RY encoding layer → CRZ     │
│                          │ entangling layer → RZ output layer) but reorganizes the 12 CRZ gates into 4 parallel      │
│                          │ sublayers using a matching decomposition of the allowed-connectivity graph (max vertex    │
│                          │ degree = 4, so 4 matchings suffice to cover all edges with no wire conflicts within a     │
│                          │ sublayer). Gates within each sublayer act on disjoint qubits and can be scheduled         │
│                          │ concurrently, which should reduce circuit depth relative to a naive sequential ordering   │
│                          │ of the same 12 gates, while keeping gate count and parameter count essentially unchanged  │
│                          │ (9 unique CRZ params via the same sharing pattern as the 0.63-scoring version:            │
│                          │ (0,7)&(0,8) share one param, (1,3)&(1,8) share one param, (2,4)&(2,6) share one param).   │
│                          │ This removes the extra CRY/RX/CCRZ layers that were shown empirically to hurt             │
│                          │ generalization, while applying the requested parallelization strategy to the entangling   │
│                          │ block.                                                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
