│ patch_name               │ hub_edge_sharing_qubit0                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the best-performing prior variant (score 0.63), this edit removes the extra   │
│                          │ `rz_pre` rotation layer that was found to hurt generalization (score dropped to 0.58 with │
│                          │ it), reverting to the leaner pre-entanglement structure. Additionally, it implements the  │
│                          │ suggested extreme hub-edge sharing: all four CRZ gates incident on qubit 0                │
│                          │ ([0,2],[0,3],[0,7],[0,8]) now share a single parameter `crz_hub0` instead of using two    │
│                          │ separate parameters (`crz_0`, `crz_1`, `crz_2` reused twice). This reduces two-qubit      │
│                          │ parameter count from 4 to 1 for qubit-0's edges, testing whether stronger symmetry-driven │
│                          │ parameter sharing (treating qubit 0 as a symmetric hub controller) improves               │
│                          │ generalization further while keeping circuit depth and gate count unchanged. The          │
│                          │ remaining CRZ sharing pattern (crz_3 for [1,3]/[1,8], crz_4 for [2,4]/[2,6]) is kept as   │
│                          │ in the best prior version, since it already demonstrated improved validation accuracy     │
│                          │ (0.72) and reduced overfitting gap (0.09) relative to the no-sharing seed.                │
