│ patch_description        │ Revert the pre-entanglement RZ layer that increased parameter count without benefit       │
│                          │ (score dropped from 0.63 to 0.58 when added), and restore the parameter-sharing CRZ       │
│                          │ pattern that achieved the best prior score (0.63). Additionally, insert a lightweight RY  │
│                          │ "refresh" layer on qubits [1,3,5,7] between the CRZ entangling block and the final RZ     │
│                          │ readout layer, as suggested. This adds only 4 new parameters/gates, giving the circuit a  │
│                          │ second amplitude-mixing stage before the final phase rotations, which may help stabilize  │
│                          │ convergence and slightly improve expressivity without significantly increasing            │
│                          │ overfitting risk (unlike the heavier rz_pre layer which hurt generalization).             │
