│ patch_name               │ crz_hub0_sharing                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Collapse all four CRZ gates incident on qubit 0 (edges [0,2], [0,3], [0,7], [0,8]) into a │
│                          │ single shared parameter `crz_hub0`. Currently these use three distinct params (crz_0,     │
│                          │ crz_1, crz_2 twice), giving qubit 0's hub asymmetric treatment relative to other qubits'  │
│                          │ more heavily shared entangling structure. Sharing a single rotation angle across all      │
│                          │ edges from qubit 0 imposes a symmetry prior (qubit 0 interacts identically with its       │
│                          │ neighbors), reducing parameter count from 162 to 159 while preserving depth and gate      │
│                          │ count. This tests whether stronger symmetry-driven parameter reduction on the             │
│                          │ highest-degree hub qubit improves generalization (smaller train-val gap) without          │
│                          │ sacrificing expressivity, following the pattern that already gave gains when moving from  │
│                          │ fully independent CRZ params (score 0.61) to partial sharing (score 0.63).                │
