│ patch_name               │ remove_zzz_add_ry_mid                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The previous experiment (0.63 score) without the three-body ZZZ layer outperformed the    │
│                          │ current version (0.58) that added it, indicating the ZZZ layer increases depth/params     │
│                          │ without benefit and likely causes overfitting/harder optimization. This edit removes the  │
│                          │ ZZZ correlation layer (reverting to the better-performing entangling structure) and       │
│                          │ instead inserts a lightweight RY mid-layer on qubits [1,3,5,7] between the CRZ block and  │
│                          │ the final RZ layer. This "RY→CRZ→RY→RZ" sandwich adds only 4 new parameters/gates, giving │
│                          │ a cheap, targeted amplitude refresh on a subset of qubits that may help convergence and   │
│                          │ expressivity without the depth/parameter cost of the ZZZ interactions.                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
