                         Patch Metadata - Gen 36/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Built directly on the best-performing prior seed (score 0.63), which used a full 12-gate  │
│                          │ parametrized CRZ entangling layer over all allowed two-qubit pairs with light, deliberate │
│                          │ parameter sharing (9 unique CRZ params instead of 12), sandwiched between an RY encoding  │
│                          │ layer and an RZ output layer. The earlier attempt to swap some CRZ gates for fixed CZ/CRX │
│                          │ gates (current program, score 0.58) hurt performance by reducing the model's entangling   │
│                          │ expressivity and breaking gate-type symmetry — confirming that fully parametrized,        │
│                          │ symmetric entangling layers are important here.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version keeps that proven full-CRZ entangling backbone intact (same 12 gates, same   │
│                          │ sharing pattern: crz_2 shared on (0,7)/(0,8), crz_3 shared on (1,3)/(1,8), crz_4 shared   │
│                          │ on (2,4)/(2,6)) but inserts a lightweight mid-layer of RY rotations on the four           │
│                          │ highest-connectivity/most "central" qubits (1, 3, 5, 7 — each touches 2-3 allowed edges)  │
│                          │ right after the entangling block and before the final RZ layer. This creates an           │
│                          │ RY(encode) → CRZ(entangle) → RY(mid-refresh) → RZ(output) sandwich. The intuition: after  │
│                          │ entanglement, a small local amplitude/phase refresh on the qubits most involved in        │
│                          │ cross-qubit interactions can help the readout layer extract better-separated features,    │
│                          │ without significantly increasing depth (+2) or parameter count (+4 unique params per      │
│                          │ repetition), and without touching the already-effective entangling structure.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a conservative, targeted modification that isolates a single new idea             │
│                          │ (recommended mid-layer RY block) on top of the known-best entangling backbone, rather     │
│                          │ than combining multiple unproven structural changes at once (as the regressed CZ/CRX      │
│                          │ variant did).                                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0577                                                                                   │
