│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ remove_zzz_reorder_crz_sublayers                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The prior experiments show that removing the three-body ZZZ correlation layer restored    │
│                          │ the best score (0.63) compared to adding it (0.58), so we revert to the simpler RY-CRZ-RZ │
│                          │ structure that performed best. On top of that, we apply the suggested optimization of     │
│                          │ reordering the twelve CRZ entangling gates into two maximally-commuting sublayers         │
│                          │ (Sublayer A on qubits with no shared wires: [0,2],[1,3],[2,4],[3,5],[5,7]; Sublayer B:    │
│                          │ [0,3],[0,7],[1,8],[2,6],[4,8],[6,7]) executing all of Sublayer A before Sublayer B. Since │
│                          │ gates within a sublayer act on disjoint qubits, they can be executed in parallel,         │
│                          │ reducing circuit depth (~39 vs 41) while keeping the same gate_count (207) and n_params   │
│                          │ (162). This should preserve or slightly improve accuracy/generalization while lowering    │
│                          │ depth, which historically correlated with better validation performance in this search.   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0336                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
