│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz swapped several CRZ entangling gates for fixed CZ gates and a CRX      │
│                          │ gate, which increased circuit depth (59 vs 41) without any parameter benefit, and         │
│                          │ empirically dropped combined score from 0.63 to 0.58 (lower train/val/test accuracy,      │
│                          │ higher losses). The earlier variant that used only parametrized CRZ gates with deliberate │
│                          │ parameter sharing (crz_2 shared for (0,7)/(0,8), crz_3 shared for (1,3)/(1,8), crz_4      │
│                          │ shared for (2,4)/(2,6)) achieved the best score so far (0.63) with fewer parameters (162) │
│                          │ and shallower depth (41). This edit reverts the entangling block to that                  │
│                          │ better-performing, parameter-efficient, shallower structure, removing the CZ/CRX          │
│                          │ substitutions and restoring full CRZ coverage with shared parameters, while keeping the   │
│                          │ same RY encoding and RZ post-rotation layers.                                             │
