│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hub0_param_collapse_on_best_topology                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The 0.63-scoring seed variant (RY layer -> CRZ layer with crz_0/crz_1/crz_2(shared over   │
│                          │ [0,7],[0,8])/crz_3(shared)/crz_4(shared)/crz_5/crz_9/crz_10/crz_11 -> RZ layer)           │
│                          │ outperformed the current 0.61-scoring "4-sublayer" variant. I revert the topology to that │
│                          │ better-performing structure, and additionally apply the recommended extreme hub-collapse: │
│                          │ all four qubit-0-incident CRZ edges ([0,2],[0,3],[0,7],[0,8]) now share a single          │
│                          │ parameter "crz_hub0" instead of three separate parameters (crz_0, crz_1, crz_2). This     │
│                          │ further reduces parameter count (from 162 to ~150 given the repetition count) while       │
│                          │ preserving the entangling connectivity and depth/gate_count, testing whether stronger     │
│                          │ symmetry around the qubit-0 hub narrows the generalization gap and improves parameter     │
│                          │ efficiency without hurting accuracy.                                                      │
