│ patch_description        │ The prior best-performing variant (score 0.63) used all-CRZ entangling gates with shared  │
│                          │ parameters on the (0,8)/(1,8)/(2,6) redundant pairs and full individual RZ                │
│                          │ post-rotations. The current variant regressed (0.59) after switching several CRZ gates to │
│                          │ CRY and merging RZ post-rotations on adjacent-index pairs (0-1,2-3,4-5,6-7). This edit    │
│                          │ reverts the CRY gates back to CRZ (restoring the higher-scoring entangling structure)     │
│                          │ while still applying end-stage parameter compression, but now using symmetric qubit-pair  │
│                          │ sharing (0↔8, 1↔7, 2↔6, 3↔5, with 4 alone) as recommended, which respects the topological │
│                          │ symmetry of the coupling map better than the previous adjacent-index merge and should     │
│                          │ preserve expressivity while cutting params from 9→5 in that layer.                        │
