│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_crz_entangling_with_rz_post_sharing                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current program replaced several CRZ entanglers with plain CZ gates, which hurt       │
│                          │ performance significantly (score dropped from 0.63 to 0.60, train/val/test accuracy all   │
│                          │ dropped ~4-8%). This confirms that parametrized CRZ entanglers on qubits (0,8), (1,8),    │
│                          │ (2,6), (5,7), (6,7) are important for this task and should not be replaced by fixed CZ    │
│                          │ gates. I'm reverting to the seed's full CRZ entangling structure (with parameter sharing  │
│                          │ on 0-hub, 1-3-8, and 2-4-6 clusters) which achieved the best score of 0.63.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On top of restoring the entangling layer, I apply the recommended post-rotation parameter │
│                          │ sharing on the final RZ layer, merging symmetric qubit pairs (0↔8, 1↔7, 2↔6, 3↔5) while   │
│                          │ leaving qubit 4 (the center) independent. This reduces RZ params from 9 to 5, cutting     │
│                          │ total parameter count from 162 to 158 without changing depth or gate count, testing       │
│                          │ whether compressing redundant end-stage phase parameters improves parameter efficiency    │
│                          │ and generalization while preserving the accuracy gains from the full CRZ entangling       │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0374                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
