│ patch_description        │ The current candidate (symmetric grouping + RX layer + ZZZ/CCRZ three-qubit gates)        │
│                          │ underperforms the original seed ansatz (0.58 vs 0.63 combined score), showing that added  │
│                          │ complexity (extra params, three-qubit gates, deeper circuit) hurt generalization rather   │
│                          │ than help it. Reverting to the original seed's proven CRZ-based structure and then        │
│                          │ applying the recommended enhancement — repeating the same 12 CRZ gates (reusing identical │
│                          │ crz_0…crz_11 parameters) right after the first CRZ block — deepens two-qubit correlations │
│                          │ without adding any new parameters. This tests whether intensifying entanglement           │
│                          │ (effectively squaring the two-qubit unitary per shared parameter) can boost               │
│                          │ expressivity/accuracy while keeping parameter count fixed at 162, potentially improving   │
│                          │ over the 0.63 baseline.                                                                   │
