│ patch_description        │ The previous edit added a mid-layer RY refresh (4 extra params) but this *decreased*      │
│                          │ combined score (0.63→0.62) and increased the generalization gap (0.09→0.10), indicating   │
│                          │ those extra single-qubit rotations added capacity without adding useful entangling        │
│                          │ structure. This edit reverts that regression by removing the mid-layer RY block, and      │
│                          │ instead invests the parameter budget more effectively by adding two three-qubit ZZZ       │
│                          │ interactions (which have no wire-pair restrictions) that link the hub qubit 0 with the    │
│                          │ two secondary clusters (qubits 4,8 and qubits 5,7). These gates share a single parameter  │
│                          │ to keep the parameter count low while introducing genuine higher-order (three-body)       │
│                          │ correlations that the existing two-qubit CRZ backbone cannot capture. Net effect versus   │
│                          │ the current program: -4 params (mid-layer RY removed) +1 param (shared ZZZ) = -3 params,  │
│                          │ while adding two three-qubit entangling gates that should improve                         │
│                          │ expressivity/generalization without ballooning the parameter count.                       │
