│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Add a lightweight RY "refresh" layer on the highest-centrality qubits (0, 2, 3, 7 — hub   │
│                          │ and cluster-connector nodes with 3+ edges in the allowed topology) inserted between the   │
│                          │ existing CRZ entangling block and the final RZ phase layer. This introduces only 4 new    │
│                          │ gates and 4 new parameters (ry_mid_0..3), keeping the parameter budget low while adding a │
│                          │ mid-circuit local mixing step. The rationale: after the CRZ entanglers act on these hub   │
│                          │ qubits, their state has accumulated entanglement-dependent phase; inserting an RY         │
│                          │ rotation lets the model locally re-mix amplitude/phase information on the qubits most     │
│                          │ involved in information flow before the final RZ readout-phase layer, potentially         │
│                          │ improving expressivity without significantly increasing overfitting risk (small parameter │
│                          │ increase, no added two/three-qubit gates).                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
