│ patch_name               │ revert_order_add_ry_refresh                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The reordered entangling-layer variant (grouped into "parallel" sublayers) underperformed │
│                          │ the original sequential CRZ ordering (0.58 vs 0.63 combined score), despite identical     │
│                          │ parameter count and gate set — indicating that the specific gate ordering affects         │
│                          │ optimization dynamics (likely due to how correlated rotations interact before commuting   │
│                          │ structure was enforced). We revert to the original, higher-performing CRZ ordering from   │
│                          │ the seed and then add a lightweight RY "refresh" layer on the four highest-centrality     │
│                          │ qubits (0, 2, 3, 7 — each participates in 3+ two-qubit gates in the entangling block)     │
│                          │ inserted between the entangling block and the final RZ phase layer. This introduces only  │
│                          │ 4 new parameters and 4 new gates (small depth increase), giving the circuit an extra      │
│                          │ chance to locally remix amplitudes on the most heavily entangled qubits before the final  │
│                          │ phase encoding, which may improve expressivity without significantly harming the          │
│                          │ train-test gap.                                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
