│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_crz_add_ry_refresh                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The previous variant that replaced several CRZ gates with plain CZ gates degraded         │
│                          │ performance (score dropped from 0.63 to 0.59), confirming that the parametrized CRZ       │
│                          │ entanglers carry useful trainable expressivity that fixed CZ gates lack. This edit        │
│                          │ reverts those CZ gates back to the original shared-parameter CRZ gates (restoring the     │
│                          │ better-performing entangling structure), and additionally inserts a lightweight RY        │
│                          │ "refresh" layer on the four highest-connectivity hub qubits (0, 2, 3, 7) between the      │
│                          │ entangling CRZ block and the final RZ phase layer. This mid-circuit local rotation lets   │
│                          │ the circuit re-mix amplitude information on the most heavily entangled qubits right after │
│                          │ they've accumulated phase from multiple CRZ interactions, before the final RZ             │
│                          │ readout-phase layer, potentially improving expressivity locally without adding            │
│                          │ significant depth or parameter overhead (only 4 extra params per repetition block).       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0339                                                                                   │
