│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zzz_cluster_link_prune_mid_ry                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The previous edit's added mid-circuit RY gates (ry_mid_0..3) increased parameter count by │
│                          │ 24 (186 vs 162) but slightly hurt validation accuracy and generalization gap versus the   │
│                          │ leaner seed variant. Revert those local single-qubit insertions and instead add genuine   │
│                          │ three-qubit entangling structure (allowed anywhere, no wire restrictions) to link the     │
│                          │ three previously disjoint entangling clusters (hub-0 cluster, 1-3-5 chain, 2-4-8 chain,   │
│                          │ and the 5-7/6-7 tail) more globally. Two ZZZ gates sharing one parameter connect qubit 0  │
│                          │ (hub) with 4 and 7 (bridging the far clusters), and connect 1, 5, 6 (bridging the chain   │
│                          │ and tail clusters). This adds richer, higher-order correlations that could better mix     │
│                          │ information across the graph while keeping the parameter budget low via aggressive        │
│                          │ sharing (only 1 new shared parameter total instead of 4 independent RY parameters         │
│                          │ removed), which should reduce overfitting risk (smaller generalization gap) while ideally │
│                          │ recovering the higher validation accuracy of the original seed.                           │
