                         Patch Metadata - Gen 60/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The previous mid-layer RY "refresh" addition regressed the combined score (0.61 vs.       │
│                          │ seed's 0.63), suggesting that a plain single-qubit rotation between the CRZ entangling    │
│                          │ layer and the final phase layer does not add useful expressivity here — it likely just    │
│                          │ adds depth/overfitting noise without capturing new correlations.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Instead, I replace that mid-layer RY block with two three-qubit ZZZ interaction gates     │
│                          │ placed on qubits that are NOT already directly coupled by the existing two-qubit CRZ      │
│                          │ backbone (0,4,6) and (1,5,8). These three-qubit gates introduce genuine higher-order      │
│                          │ (three-body) correlations among the encoded features that pairwise CRZ gates cannot       │
│                          │ capture, while only adding 2 new parameters (with no sharing needed since each triple is  │
│                          │ independent) and 2 gates — a much smaller footprint than the previous 4-gate RY refresh.  │
│                          │ This should improve model capacity/train accuracy while keeping the generalization gap    │
│                          │ controlled, since three-qubit gates concentrated on previously-unconnected qubit triples  │
│                          │ add complementary information rather than redundant rotations on already-entangled wires. │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0579                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 0; deleted: 3; modified: 5;                                                        │
