                         Patch Metadata - Gen 61/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two best-performing seed ansätze (score 0.63) with the mid-layer-refresh │
│                          │ variant (score 0.61). Analysis of the metrics shows: (1) the clean seed structure — RY    │
│                          │ encoding, a CRZ entangling backbone with light, deliberate parameter sharing across       │
│                          │ symmetric edges, followed by an *individually parametrized* RZ output layer — outperforms │
│                          │ the variant that (a) inserted extra mid-circuit RY refresh rotations and (b) shared the   │
│                          │ final RZ parameters across wire pairs (0.61 vs 0.63, higher depth/gate-count, worse       │
│                          │ validation accuracy and gap). So we discard the mid-layer RY refresh and the shared       │
│                          │ post-RZ scheme, restoring the proven backbone.                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To still search for improvement (rather than just reproducing the seed), we add a         │
│                          │ lightweight three-qubit ZZZ interaction layer that captures higher-order correlations     │
│                          │ across the two loosely-coupled "sub-clusters" of the entangling graph (qubits {0,4,6},    │
│                          │ {1,2,5}, {3,7,8}, chosen to be disjoint and to cover every qubit exactly once). All three │
│                          │ ZZZ gates share a single parameter, adding just 1 extra parameter (163 total) while       │
│                          │ giving the circuit access to triple-qubit correlations that pure two-qubit CRZ entanglers │
│                          │ cannot represent, potentially improving expressivity/accuracy without notably increasing  │
│                          │ depth or parameter count (three-qubit gates are unrestricted in wire choice per the       │
│                          │ schema). The final individually-parametrized RZ output layer (9 unique params) is kept    │
│                          │ intact, since that was the differentiator that made the seed outperform its variant.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This aims to combine the proven strong structure with a minimal, targeted structural      │
│                          │ addition to explore for further gains in validation accuracy / generalization gap without │
│                          │ materially increasing depth or gate count.                                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
