│ patch_name               │ encoding_param_sharing_revert_mid                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Two changes: (1) Revert the mid-circuit RY rejuvenation layer added in the previous       │
│                          │ iteration, since it increased parameter count (186) and depth without improving           │
│                          │ accuracy—validation accuracy dropped from 0.72 to 0.68 and score from 0.63 to 0.60.       │
│                          │ Reverting restores the better-performing architecture. (2) Apply light parameter sharing  │
│                          │ in the initial encoding layer: pair ry_1 with wire 8 (both use param "ry_1") and ry_3     │
│                          │ with wire 6 (both use param "ry_3"), removing the previously separate ry_6 and ry_8       │
│                          │ parameters. This reduces total parameter count by 2 (from 162 to 160 in the reverted      │
│                          │ architecture) while keeping full expressivity of feature encoding across all 9 qubits,    │
│                          │ testing whether this tighter parameterization improves the train-test gap and parameter   │
│                          │ efficiency without harming accuracy, consistent with the recommendation to explore        │
│                          │ limited encoding-layer sharing.                                                           │
