│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover keeps the proven high-performing backbone from the two 0.63-scoring seeds  │
│                          │ (RY encoding → hub-and-cluster CRZ entangling layer with partial parameter sharing on the │
│                          │ two 4-connectivity qubits (0-7/0-8) and the two symmetric pairs (1-3/1-8, 2-4/2-6) →      │
│                          │ independent RZ post-rotation), since removing the earlier pre-entangling RZ layer and     │
│                          │ de-sharing most CRZ parameters was what drove the score up from 0.54 to 0.63.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ On top of that stable backbone, two lightweight additions are introduced to boost         │
│                          │ expressibility and capture higher-order correlations without materially inflating the     │
│                          │ parameter/gate budget:                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. A cheap RX "pre-tilt" layer between the RY encoding and the CRZ entangling layer, with │
│                          │ qubits grouped into 3 sets of 3 (by index mod 3) sharing one parameter each. This gives   │
│                          │ every qubit a second rotation axis (Y then X) before entangling, at the cost of only 3    │
│                          │ extra parameters per block, which should help the circuit represent richer single-qubit   │
│                          │ states without adding much overfitting risk.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. A single three-qubit CCRZ gate on well-separated qubits (0, 4, 8) placed after the     │
│                          │ pairwise CRZ layer, adding one more parameter per block to let the model capture a        │
│                          │ genuine three-body correlation that pairwise gates cannot express, again at minimal       │
│                          │ parameter cost.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The final independent RZ post-rotation layer (one free parameter per qubit) is kept       │
│                          │ unchanged from the best-performing seed, preserving per-qubit phase flexibility for the   │
│                          │ readout.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design tries to combine the empirically best entangling/readout structure with a     │
│                          │ modest, cheaply-parameterized boost in expressibility (extra rotation axis + one          │
│                          │ higher-order interaction), aiming to push validation accuracy higher while keeping the    │
│                          │ train-validation gap and parameter count under control.                                   │
