│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sym_share_rz_post                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Apply symmetric parameter sharing to the final RZ layer: rz_post_i shares its parameter   │
│                          │ with rz_post_{8-i} for i=0..3, leaving rz_post_4 as the unique center parameter. This     │
│                          │ reduces the RZ layer from 9 unique parameters to 5, cutting total parameter count by 4    │
│                          │ (186→182) while preserving circuit depth and gate count. The idea is that the trailing    │
│                          │ local phase layer likely encodes some qubit-symmetric structure (mirrored roles of qubit  │
│                          │ pairs relative to the hub qubit 0), so tying mirrored phases together should reduce       │
│                          │ overfitting/gap without harming expressivity much, consistent with the recommendation to  │
│                          │ test if compressing end-stage phases tightens the generalization gap.                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0251                                                                                   │
