│                          │ increased the parameter count (162→186) and circuit depth (41→47), but *decreased*        │
│                          │ combined score from 0.63 to 0.60 along with worse validation accuracy (0.72→0.68) and     │
│                          │ test accuracy (0.65→0.63). This strongly suggests the extra mid-layer adds                │
│                          │ noise/overfitting risk without benefit given the fixed training budget. Reverting to the  │
│                          │ leaner seed structure (no mid-layer) restores the better-performing configuration, while  │
│                          │ keeping the well-tested CRZ entangling structure intact. This also aligns with the        │
│                          │ recommendation to keep depth lean; removing the mid-layer directly reduces depth by ~4-6  │
│                          │ layers and drops 24 unnecessary parameters, improving parameter efficiency without        │
│                          │ touching the entangling topology that was already shown to generalize better.             │
