│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover between the two 0.63-scoring seed variants (RY encoding + CRZ backbone with     │
│                          │ symmetric parameter sharing + RZ post-rotations) and the ZZZ-augmented variant (0.62)     │
│                          │ that showed a test-accuracy gain from adding three-qubit correlation terms but suffered   │
│                          │ validation loss/gap due to the added depth of three separate ZZZ gates (each spanning all │
│                          │ 9 qubits, tripling the added depth/gate-count).                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This version keeps the proven, low-depth CRZ backbone exactly as in the best-scoring      │
│                          │ seeds (identical structure and parameter sharing, which reached validation_accuracy 0.72  │
│                          │ and the best combined score of 0.63), and reintroduces only a *single* ZZZ three-qubit    │
│                          │ correlation gate (instead of three), placed on well-separated hub qubits (0, 4, 7) that   │
│                          │ already participate in multiple two-qubit connections in the backbone. This adds just one │
│                          │ extra gate and one extra parameter per repetition, giving the model the extra correlation │
│                          │ capacity that boosted test accuracy in the previous experiment, while keeping the depth   │
│                          │ and gate-count increase to roughly a third of what the 3xZZZ version incurred — aiming to │
│                          │ capture the upside (better test/generalization) without the downside (extra depth hurting │
│                          │ validation).                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Everything else (encoding layer, post-rotation layer, no shared params except within the  │
│                          │ CRZ backbone as in the original seed) is kept unchanged to preserve the well-performing   │
│                          │ baseline.                                                                                 │
