│ patch_description        │ The suggested recommendation to add CRZ gates on edges [1,5] and [2,3] is not             │
│                          │ implementable because those qubit pairs are not in the allowed two-qubit connectivity     │
│                          │ list. To achieve the same underlying goal—densifying the secondary cluster region (qubits │
│                          │ 1,2,3,5,6) with a modest number of extra parameters/gates—we instead use two three-qubit  │
│                          │ ZZZ gates (which have no wire restriction) that touch the same secondary-cluster qubits   │
│                          │ and share a single new parameter "zzz_sec". This adds richer triple-wise correlations     │
│                          │ among the already-entangled secondary cluster (1-3, 2-4/2-6, 3-5) without increasing      │
│                          │ depth much (+2 gates, +1 param), keeping the parameter count close to the current         │
│                          │ 162-param sweet spot while testing whether extra multi-qubit correlations in that region  │
│                          │ improve validation/test accuracy and reduce the generalization gap further.               │
