│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sparse_ry_sharing_encoding                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce parameter count in the encoding layer by sharing RY parameters across pairs of     │
│                          │ qubits that are already coupled downstream in the entangling layer: ry_1↔ry_8 (qubits 1   │
│                          │ and 8 are directly connected via crz_3) and ry_3↔ry_6 (qubits 3 and 6 share structurally  │
│                          │ similar roles in the hub connectivity). This mirrors the successful parameter-sharing     │
│                          │ philosophy already used in the CRZ entangling layer, cutting encoding params from 9 to 7  │
│                          │ (total n_params from 162 to ~160), which should slightly improve parameter efficiency and │
│                          │ possibly reduce overfitting (train-test gap) without significantly harming expressivity,  │
│                          │ since the shared qubits play structurally symmetric roles in the circuit.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0483                                                                                   │
