│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sparse_encoding_param_sharing                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce the encoding layer's parameter count by sharing RY feature-rotation parameters     │
│                          │ across pairs of qubits that are already entangled together downstream (1&8 via crz_3, and │
│                          │ 3&6 which are both targets of crz_1/crz_4 chains respectively). This compresses the       │
│                          │ encoding from 9 independent parameters to 7, lowering total n_params from 162 to 160,     │
│                          │ while testing whether the shared structure (feature qubits that later interact) preserves │
│                          │ expressivity. Since qubits 1/8 and 3/6 already end up correlated through the entangling   │
│                          │ layer, tying their initial rotation angles is a natural low-risk way to cut parameters    │
│                          │ without breaking the circuit's information flow, potentially improving parameter          │
│                          │ efficiency and reducing overfitting (train-test gap) while maintaining accuracy.          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
