│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ rx_mid_refresh_hub0                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add a single lightweight RX "refresh" gate on the hub qubit (wire 0) right after the CRZ  │
│                          │ entangling block and before the final RZ output layer. Qubit 0 acts as the central hub    │
│                          │ with the most connections (4 CRZ gates), so its state has accumulated the most            │
│                          │ entanglement-induced phase. Injecting a fresh RX rotation there (a different axis than    │
│                          │ the RZ before/after) mixes amplitude components at the most information-dense node,       │
│                          │ potentially improving expressivity and gradient flow with minimal cost (+1 param, +1      │
│                          │ gate, +1 depth). This is a cheap, targeted change consistent with prior                   │
│                          │ parameter-efficiency goals.                                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
