│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ remove_rx_shared_add_mid_rx_refresh                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The previous edit added a shared-parameter RX layer duplicating the RY parameters before  │
│                          │ entanglement, which increased depth/gate count and slightly hurt validation/test accuracy │
│                          │ (0.62 vs 0.63 baseline) without adding parameters. This edit reverts that costly change   │
│                          │ (removing the 9 extra RX gates) and instead inserts a single, cheap mid-circuit RX        │
│                          │ "refresh" gate on the hub qubit 0 right after the CRZ entangling block. This targets the  │
│                          │ qubit with the highest connectivity (crz_0, crz_1, crz_2 all originate from wire 0) with  │
│                          │ a fresh local rotation to help re-align amplitude before the final RZ readout layer,      │
│                          │ adding only 1 gate and 1 parameter instead of 9 gates with 0 new parameters. This should  │
│                          │ restore the previous best performance while testing whether a lightweight, localized      │
│                          │ injection can further improve gradient flow at the entanglement hub without the           │
│                          │ depth/gate-count penalty of the full shared RX layer.                                     │
