│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sparse_encoding_param_sharing                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce the encoding layer's parameter count by sharing RY parameters between pairs of     │
│                          │ qubits that are already connected in the entangling layers: ry_1↔ry_8 (linked via crz_3   │
│                          │ on wires [1,8]) and ry_3↔ry_6 (both connect to hub qubits 0/2 through crz_1/crz_4         │
│                          │ respectively). This is a structured compression—unlike random parameter tying, these      │
│                          │ pairs are chosen because they participate in shared entangling gates, so tying their      │
│                          │ encoding rotations reinforces a symmetry the entangler already exploits, rather than      │
│                          │ fighting it. This drops encoding params from 9 to 7 (total n_params from 162 to 160),     │
│                          │ slightly easing the optimization landscape and potentially reducing overfitting           │
│                          │ (train-test gap) while testing whether expressivity is preserved given the seed's stable  │
│                          │ 0.72 validation accuracy.                                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0223                                                                                   │
