│ patch_name               │ revert_zzz_add_crz_dense                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The previous edit that added two ZZZ three-qubit interactions to the secondary cluster    │
│                          │ regressed performance (score 0.59 vs 0.63 baseline), likely due to increased              │
│                          │ depth/parameter count without a corresponding gain in expressivity for this data. This    │
│                          │ edit reverts that change and instead follows the hub-and-spoke densification              │
│                          │ recommendation: replace the ZZZ block with two additional CRZ entanglers on the secondary │
│                          │ cluster (wires (1,5) and (2,3)), sharing a single new parameter "crz_12". This keeps the  │
│                          │ two-qubit-gate-only structure (which scored better empirically), adds modest connectivity │
│                          │ between the two chains (1-3-5 and 2-4-6/8), and only increases parameter count by 1 while │
│                          │ adding 2 gates, in contrast to the previous edit's use of unrestricted-but-costly 3-qubit │
│                          │ gates.                                                                                    │
