│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This candidate is a crossover between the two best-performing seeds (score 0.63) and the  │
│                          │ more elaborate cycle/chord/CCRZ variant (score 0.58). It keeps the proven low-depth       │
│                          │ "hub-qubit-0 + secondary cluster" CRZ entangling topology from the 0.63 seed (which gave  │
│                          │ the best generalization gap and validation accuracy), since that structure clearly        │
│                          │ outperformed the higher-depth cycle-based design. On top of that stable backbone we graft │
│                          │ two targeted improvements inspired by the second program:                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Parameter-efficient mirrored final RZ phase layer (rz_post_0..rz_post_4 shared         │
│                          │ symmetrically across "mirror" qubits by distance from the hub), cutting the number of     │
│                          │ independent output-phase parameters roughly in half versus the 9 independent RZ's in the  │
│                          │ top seed, improving parameter efficiency without removing any gates from the circuit      │
│                          │ (gate count/depth unchanged).                                                             │
│                          │ 2. A single, cheap three-qubit CCRZ correlation gate (on qubits that are maximally        │
│                          │ separated in the entangling graph: 0, 4, 7) borrowed from the cycle-based program, added  │
│                          │ once (not twice) to inject a small amount of higher-order correlation while keeping added │
│                          │ depth minimal (only one extra multi-qubit gate instead of two CCRZ + extra CRX chords     │
│                          │ that hurt the other candidate).                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the low depth/gate-count profile that correlated with the higher score while   │
│                          │ cautiously adding expressiveness and trimming redundant post-processing parameters.       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0549                                                                                   │
