│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ seed_plus_zzz_cross_cluster                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The prior sublayer-based CRZ regrouping (current file, score 0.62) underperformed the     │
│                          │ original seed ordering (score 0.63) despite using the same total gate set — evidence that │
│                          │ gate *ordering* and clustering (not just connectivity) matters here, likely due to how    │
│                          │ partial cancellations/interference build up along the circuit. This edit reverts the      │
│                          │ entangling block to the seed's proven ordering (hub-qubit-0 first, then 1-3-5/2-4-8       │
│                          │ chains, then 5-7/6-7 closing gates) and additionally injects a single three-qubit ZZZ     │
│                          │ interaction across three previously only pairwise-connected clusters (qubits 0, 4, 7 —    │
│                          │ each a hub/bridge qubit in the existing topology). Three-qubit gates are unrestricted in  │
│                          │ wire choice, so this creates a genuinely new higher-order correlation that pairwise CRZ   │
│                          │ chains cannot capture, at the cost of just one extra parameter and one extra gate. This   │
│                          │ should help capture interactions between the hub cluster (0), the 2-4-8 chain, and the    │
│                          │ 5-7/6-7 closing cluster without expanding two-qubit connectivity or param count           │
│                          │ significantly, targeting improved validation accuracy while keeping the train-test gap    │
│                          │ and parameter budget in check.                                                            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0476                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
