                         Patch Metadata - Gen 79/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz only captures pairwise correlations between qubits (via CRZ on the 12  │
│                          │ allowed edges). To let the circuit model higher-order (three-body) correlations that no   │
│                          │ single two-qubit gate pair can express, I insert three disjoint CCRZ                      │
│                          │ (controlled-controlled-RZ) gates on triples of qubits: (0,4,6), (1,5,7), (2,3,8). These   │
│                          │ three triples partition all 9 qubits and are mutually disjoint in wires, so they can be   │
│                          │ executed in parallel, adding essentially only one extra layer of depth rather than three. │
│                          │ All three CCRZ gates share a single parameter name ("ccrz_0"), so only one new trainable  │
│                          │ parameter is introduced (162→163), keeping the parameter budget essentially unchanged     │
│                          │ while enriching the expressivity of the ansatz. This is placed after the two-qubit        │
│                          │ entangling sublayers and before the final local RZ phases, so the newly created           │
│                          │ three-body correlations are read out through the following single-qubit rotations. This   │
│                          │ should help close the generalization gap and lift both validation and test accuracy       │
│                          │ without meaningfully increasing circuit depth or parameter count.                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0751                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 0.5                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 7; deleted: 0; modified: 0;                                                        │
